# Objective: Port TrueVision's Full PBR Render System into ValeVision 3D as a Selectable Second Render Engine.

## Engine Definitions

### ValeVision PureEngine (current — always the default)
ValeVision's existing render pipeline. It must **never change** as part of this task. Every existing project uses PureEngine and will continue to do so unless a developer explicitly opts a model into MaxEngine.

PureEngine render pass order (current):
1. RenderPass — renders scene to colour RT
2. Profile Lines — architectural edge outlines (optional, configurable)
3. Fog — distance-based atmospheric haze (optional, configurable)
4. FXAA — fast approximate anti-aliasing

PureEngine materials: ValeVision whitecard (no PBR, no materials library, no textures).

### ValeVision MaxEngine (to be built — optional, per-model opt-in)
The full TrueVision-equivalent render pipeline. Adds SSAO, PBR materials hot-swapping, glass rendering, and AO layer exclusion.

MaxEngine render pass order (from TrueVision):
1. RenderPass
2. Profile Lines (same as PureEngine)
3. Fog (same as PureEngine)
4. SSAO — screen-space ambient occlusion
5. AO Blur — 5×5 Gaussian to smooth AO noise
6. FXAA

MaxEngine materials: full PBR via `Na__MaterialsSystem__MaterialSwap.js`, driven by `Na__AppConfig__MaterialsLibrary.json` and the remote Na__DataLib (fetched at runtime from GitHub). Supports `MeshStandardMaterial` with roughness, metalness, envMap, textures, glass (transparent / double-sided), and AO layer exclusion (foliage on Three.js layer 1).

