## Folder Architecture (Critical — Do Not Violate)

The two engines must live in separate, clearly bounded subfolders within `05__RenderPipeline/`. No file from one engine's subfolder should be imported by the other engine's subfolder. The shared pipeline infrastructure (render loop invalidation, profile lines, fog) lives in the parent `05__RenderPipeline/` folder and is imported by both engines.

Proposed structure:
```
02__Src__AppModules/
  05__RenderPipeline/
    01__Engine__PureEngine/
      Na__RenderPipeline__PureEngine__Setup.js     ← current PostProcessing__Setup.js, renamed + re-headered
    02__Engine__MaxEngine/
      Na__RenderPipeline__MaxEngine__Setup.js      ← ported + adapted from TrueVision PostProcessing__Setup.js
    Na__RenderEffect__ProfileLines__.js            ← shared (unchanged)
    Na__RenderLoop__Invalidation.js                ← shared (unchanged)
  07__Scene__EnvironmentEffects/                   ← new folder (port from TrueVision)
      Na__RenderEffect__AmbientOcclusion__.js      ← SSAO pass (MaxEngine only)
      Na__RenderEffect__AmbientOcclusion__Shader.js← SSAO GLSL shader (MaxEngine only)
  20__System__MaterialsSystem/
      Na__MaterialsSystem__MaterialSwap.js         ← already exists; activated only by MaxEngine
      Na__MaterialsSystem__LibraryLoader.js        ← already exists; activated only by MaxEngine
  01__AppCore/
      AppCore__DataLib__Loader.js                  ← new; port from TrueVision (fetches Na__DataLib from GitHub)
```

A new `.mdc` rule file must be created at `.cursor/rules/07-RenderEngine-Architecture-.mdc` that documents this two-engine design and instructs agents to never merge engine-specific code across folders or activate MaxEngine-only systems (SSAO, DataLib, MaterialSwap) from PureEngine paths.

