## Conclusion
When complete: in ValeVision localhost mode, a new **"Render Engine"** Dev menu section lets the developer switch the current model between PureEngine (default, unchanged whitecard) and MaxEngine (full PBR, SSAO, materials hot-swap, glass). The choice is saved to `project.json` via the standard Dev save pattern. When a user views the model in production, if MaxEngine is saved for that model, they see the full PBR render quality with the ability to switch back to PureEngine from the Tools & Settings menu. If MaxEngine is not enabled for a model, the Tools & Settings "Render Engine" section is invisible and the user experience is identical to the current ValeVision. All existing models remain on PureEngine by default with zero visible change.

